1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
JAPANESE FILM DIALOGUE: Yamete. / “Stop.”

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A character says “stop.” What can that word actually change?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
This is film dialogue, not off-camera proof. Later comes a public negotiation.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
LATER IN THE FILM · PUBLIC PERFORMANCE

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,650
VOICE IN THE PERFORMANCE: Is there anyone who wants to come up and hit Jiarui?

6
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:18,450
VOICE IN THE PERFORMANCE: Raise your hand.

7
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:19,350
AUDIENCE: Can we hit him?

8
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:20,250
VOICE IN THE PERFORMANCE: You can hit him.

9
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,250
AUDIENCE: As much as we want?

10
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:21,950
VOICE IN THE PERFORMANCE: Yes.

11
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:24,767
JIARUI — NAME USED IN THE FILM: But I will fight back.

12
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:30,500
Permission is given twice. Then comes the answer: “But I will fight back.”

13
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Permission for one thing is not permission for everything.

14
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,500
A usable “stop” must be able to change the scene.

15
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,500
